+function Select-PriceTableWinner {
+  <#
+    .SYNOPSIS The ONE row that represents a store's everyday half, or its live-ad half.
+    .DESCRIPTION This was `Sort-Object unit_price | Select-Object -First 1`, and Windows PowerShell 5.1's
+                 Sort-Object is NOT stable (no -Stable switch before PowerShell 6), so whenever two rows
+                 tied on unit price the PRODUCT this table named was chosen by the sort's internals and
+                 could differ from the one the board named for the same store (backlog I175). Measured on
